==Major events==
{{spoilers}}
* {{p|Celebi}} is captured in a [[GS Ball]] by Pryce.
* The Johto Pokédex holders go back in time to catch [[Pryce]].
* Pryce and Gold get stuck in time, but only Gold manages to escape.
* The Pokédex holders (that didn't know already) learn that {{Adv|Yellow}} is a girl.
* Gold is no longer frozen in time.
* [[Kanto]] Gym Leaders are recognized to have beaten [[Johto]] Gym Leaders in the tournament.
* The Pokémon League is suspended from the damaged state that the entire fiasco left it in.
* {{Adv|Ruby}} moves from [[Johto]] to [[Littleroot Town]] in [[Hoenn]].
* Ruby meets [[Professor Birch]].
* Ruby meets {{Adv|Sapphire}}.
* Ruby and Sapphire make a bet to see who can beat their [[Ribbon|respective]] [[Badge|goals]] in eighty days.
* Norman is informed of Ruby's running away and decides to search for his son.
* {{Adv|Sapphire}} goes on her journey to challenge the Hoenn's Gyms.
* {{Adv|Ruby}} meets {{adv|Wally}}.
* Ruby helps Wally capture his first Pokémon, a {{p|Kecleon}}.
* Ruby is swept out to sea after an earthquake and loses his {{p|Ralts}}. This Ralts is later found by {{adv|Wally}}.
* {{adv|Sapphire}} defeats [[Team Aqua]], but they successfully steal the [[Devon Parts|Devon Goods]].
* [[Mr. Stone]] gives {{adv|Sapphire}} a letter for {{Steven}}.
* {{Adv|Ruby}} is rescued by [[Mr. Briney]] at sea.

==Party changes==
===Additions===
*Ruby's {{p|Mudkip}}, "[[Mumu]]" in [[PS183]].

===Evolutions===
* No Pokémon evolve in this volume.

==Gym battles==
* {{Adv|Sapphire}} begins her battle with [[Roxanne]] in [[PS190]].

==Pokémon Contests==
{{adv|Ruby}} doesn't participate in any Pokémon Contests.

==Trivia==
===Localization===
The cover art for this volume was changed from the original in the [[VIZ Media]] release. As their release of this volume did not include ''[[PS180|The Last Battle XIV]]'', due to it being published in {{PAV|14}}, the new front cover design was meant to omit the previous main characters to disassociate the {{MangaArc|Ruby & Sapphire}} from the previous arcs. The new back cover has the picture of [[Pryce]] replaced with the picture of Ruby and the Hoenn [[first partner Pokémon]] from the original front cover design.

In {{pmin|Germany}} and {{pmin|the Netherlands}}, this volume was split in two between the {{MangaArc2|Gold, Silver & Crystal}} and {{MangaArc2|Ruby & Sapphire}} arcs.

